# Claude Instructions

- Use `uv sync` to install dependencies and `uv run` for all project commands.
- Organize code using the existing layering: `application` (models, schemas, services, dependencies), `core` (config, logging{% if enable_telemetry %}, telemetry{% endif %}), `database` (session, queues{% if include_example_endpoint %}, repositories{% endif %}), and `api` (routers).
- Do not bypass dependency injection; the `ServiceContainer` shape lives in `container.py`, built by `bootstrap.py`. Extend both together, and keep `container.py` free of runtime imports from `application`/`database` (`TYPE_CHECKING` only) — that's what keeps `application/dependencies.py` from having to import the whole service graph just to type-hint the container.
- Add or update scopes through `Settings.scopes` and `ScopeRegistry`.
- Keep request handlers non-blocking and move long-running work to the configured queue backend.
- `azure-storage-queue` is an optional dependency (the `azure` extra); `database/queues.py` imports it lazily. Don't move that import back to module scope.
{% if enable_azure_auth -%}
- This service is a resource server for Azure Entra ID: `core/auth.py` builds `azure_scheme` from the container's settings (not a module-level singleton, so `create_app(settings=...)` overrides actually take effect), and `get_current_user` resolves the caller from it. Depend on `CurrentUserDep` for "any valid caller" and `require_role("X")` (see `require_admin_role`) for app-role checks — don't hand-roll JWT parsing. `require_role` is `get_current_user` wired to the provider-agnostic `check_role(role, user)`, which only assumes `user.roles`; a future non-Entra provider reuses `check_role` and just supplies its own identity dependency. Tests override `get_current_user` via `app.dependency_overrides`, never real tokens. New routers must add `dependencies=[Depends(get_current_user)]` themselves — enabling Azure auth only protects routers that declare it.
{% endif -%}
- Maintain Google-style docstrings with explicit types.
{% if enable_telemetry -%}
- Keep tracing enabled through `core/telemetry.py` and trace-aware logging through `core/logging.py`.
{% else -%}
- OpenTelemetry is disabled for this project (`enable_telemetry=false`); `core/logging.py` only injects the correlation ID, not trace/span IDs.
{% endif -%}
- Refresh `.claude/skills` and `.agents/skills` with `uv run library-skills --tool-skill install --claude --yes --all` after dependency changes.
- Type-check with `pyright` (standard mode), not mypy or `ty`.
